#%PAM-1.0
# swaylock: unlock = FIDO2 key + its client PIN + touch.
#
# Do NOT stack pam_unix here: swaylock hands the one typed secret to every PAM
# prompt, so the key PIN and the account password would have to be identical.
# Flow: type the key PIN, Enter, touch the key when it blinks.
#
# The mapping file is root-owned so a compromised user session cannot add a key.
# Once a fingerprint is enrolled on the key (fido2-token -S -e <dev>), replace
# pinverification=1 with userverification=1 for fingerprint + touch.
auth     required  pam_u2f.so authfile=/etc/u2f_mappings cue origin=pam://workstation appid=pam://workstation pinverification=1 userpresence=1 max_devices=4
account  include   login
